      "channel": "pipeline",
      "channel_name": "Request Pipeline",
      "purpose_class": "deliberation",
      "purpose": "Write ordering: the gap between handing a batch to the provider and writing anything down",
      "reason": "emil found three batches on the OpenAI dashboard that finished and were paid for with no local record of them at all",
      "expected_outcome": "dermot's ordering is the working plan but nobody has written it down as a decision; dario wants to check whether the batch submit call is even awaited per-batch or fired in a gather; it is settled that the team agrees writing run state only after the download completes leaves the entire polling window unrecoverable",
      "agenda": [
        "emil on the orphans: they were submitted, the process died before the first poll came back, and nothing on disk mentioned them",
        "dario says today the tracker only gets written once the poll loop has a status to record, which is why the ids evaporated",
        "dermot suggests the id gets appended and flushed the moment the provider returns it, before any polling starts, so the worst case is a record with no status yet"
      ],
      "subjects": [
        "batch_objects.jsonl",
        "OpenAI batch dashboard",
        "submit_batch",
        "poll loop"
