        {
          "clue": "t3.r1.L5",
          "kind": "clue",
          "holder": "dario",
          "text": "All the wall clock in a batch run is the poll loop. Submit at 11, provider finishes somewhere around 6, and the only moment we write anything durable is after the download comes back. Kill it at hour three and there is nothing on disk that so much as knows a job was ever opened. That bit me twice this week.",
          "settles": "the team agrees writing run state only after the download completes leaves the entire polling window unrecoverable",
          "verbatim": [],
